    "type": "agent_text",
    "text": "I've read the part. Before I set up the solve, I need you to confirm a few inputs.\n\n**What the part looks like**\n- **Base plate:** a flat plate about 64 mm \u00d7 64 mm \u00d7 12.7 mm, lying in the XZ plane with its underside at y = 0.\n- **Upright wall:** a 12.7 mm thick web rising from the plate to y = 38.1 mm, on the plate's near edge.\n- **Four base holes:** 10.2 mm diameter, running through the plate at its four corners (faces 0:56, 0:59, 0:62, 0:65, 0:86, 0:89, 0:92, 0:95).\n- **Centre hole:** about 12.7 mm diameter, through the upright wall near its top (faces 0:38 and 0:98).\n- **Sharp inside corners:** four, where the wall meets the plate top. The two 38.1 mm corners (0:50/0:71 and 0:44/0:71) carry the main load path, so they need fillets before any stress result can be trusted.\n- **Baseline mass:** 0.447 kg (structural steel, default).\n\n**Proposed load case (please confirm or correct)**\n- **Fixed faces:** the eight half-cylinder faces of the four base holes.\n- **Load faces:** the two half-cylinder faces of the centre hole (0:38 and 0:98).\n- **Force:** 5000 N in the +y direction (up, away from the base plate), i.e. [0, 5000, 0] N.\n- **Material:** Structural Steel (ANSYS library default). Say if you meant a different steel.\n\n**Safety factor**\nYou asked for 0.8. Safety factor is yield strength divided by peak von Mises stress, so 0.8 allows the peak stress to be about 1.25 times the yield strength. At that point the part has yielded, and a linear-elastic solve is no longer a valid check. Is 0.8 deliberate, or did you mean the 1.5 default? If 0.8 is right, I'll run it as asked but flag the yielding in every result.\n\n**Fillets (proposed)**\nI suggest a 5 mm fillet radius on all four inside corners, so the peak stress is a real converged value. You can change the radius.\n\n**Objective and limits**\nYou want minimum mass. Do you have a maximum deflection at the centre hole, or only the stress limit from the safety factor? If there's no deflection limit, I'll use only the stress limit.\n\nOnce you confirm the load case, material, safety factor and fillet radius, I'll set the load case, evaluate the baseline, and run a mesh check on it."
